--TEST--
`Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::properties` names every property a class declares and `Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo` carries the visibility and the declared type of each — `rule:core-classes/reflect` and `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::properties
// covers: Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::hasProperty
// covers: Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo::name
// covers: Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo::isPublic
// `rule:core-classes/reflect`: reading a member's *shape* — that it exists, what it is
// called, what type it holds, what it may be reached from — is introspection
// and is always available. Acting on one is the other half, and it is
// `Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::get`'s, not this roster's.
class Account {
    public string $owner = "ada";
    public ?int $limit = null;
    private int $secret = 7;
}

var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject(new Account());
var $roster = $described->properties();

// All three, slot order, each row a `Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo`. The count is
// asserted beside the names because a roster that dropped the `private` one
// still prints two plausible lines.
echo Core\Arr::count($roster), "\n";
foreach ($roster as Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo $property) {
    echo $property->name(), " ", $property->isPublic() ? "public" : "closed", " ",
         $property->type() ?? "none", "\n";
}

// `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`: the `private` property is named and its bit says
// so — the visibility travels with the row rather than deciding whether there
// is a row. Nothing here reaches a value: a name, a bit and a written type are
// what the declaration already published.
echo $described->hasProperty("secret") ? "declared" : "absent", "\n";
echo $described->hasProperty("owner") ? "declared" : "absent", "\n";

// And a name the class declares nothing of. `rule:core-classes/reflect` asks that a refusal be
// distinguishable from a misspelling, which is exactly the difference between
// the two lines above and this one.
echo $described->hasProperty("balance") ? "declared" : "absent", "\n";
--EXPECT--
3
owner public string
limit public ?int
secret closed int
declared
declared
absent
